      "text": "that thy whole body should be cast into hell, Matt. 5:29. Take no thought … for your body, what ye shall put on, Matt. 6:25 (Luke 12:22). fear not them which kill the body, Matt. 10:28 (Luke 12:4). Take, eat; this is my body, Matt. 26:26 (Mark 14:22; Luke 22:19; 1 Cor. 11:24). many bodies of the saints which slept arose, Matt. 27:52. He went to Pilate, and begged the body of Jesus, Matt. 27:58 (Mark 15:43; Luke 23:52; John 19:38). Wheresoever the body is, thither will the eagles be, Luke 17:37. found not the body of the Lord Jesus, Luke 24:3. he spake of the temple of his body, John 2:21. that the bodies should not remain upon the cross, John 19:31. Peter … turning him to the body said, Tabitha, Acts 9:40. gave them up … to dishonour their own bodies, Rom. 1:24. become dead to the law by the body of Christ, Rom. 7:4. the body is dead because of sin, Rom. 8:10. for the adoption, to wit, the redemption of our body, Rom. 8:23. we, being many, are one body in Christ, Rom. 12:5 (1 Cor. 10:17). absent in body, but present in spirit, 1 Cor. 5:3. your bodies are the members of Christ, 1 Cor. 6:15. wife hath not power of her own body, 1 Cor. 7:4. she may be holy both in body and in spirit, 1 Cor. 7:34. I keep under my body, and bring it into subjection, 1 Cor. 9:27. communion of the body of Christ, 1 Cor. 10:16. guilty of the body and blood of the Lord, 1 Cor. 11:27. by one Spirit are we all baptized into one body, 1 Cor. 12:13. ye are the body of Christ, 1 Cor. 12:27. raised up? and with what body do they come, 1 Cor. 15:35. also celestial bodies, and bodies terrestrial, 1 Cor. 15:40 (D&C 76:70, 78). sown a natural body; it is raised a spiritual body, 1 Cor. 15:44. whether in the body, or out of the body, I cannot tell, 2 Cor. 12:3 (D&C 137:1). bear in my body the marks of the Lord Jesus, Gal. 6:17. reconcile both unto God in one body by the cross, Eph. 2:16. There is one body, and one Spirit, Eph. 4:4. he is the saviour of the body, Eph. 5:23. men to love their wives as their own bodies, Eph. 5:28. change our vile body … like unto his glorious body, Philip. 3:21. he is the head of the body, Col. 1:18. spirit and soul and body be preserved blameless, 1 Thes. 5:23. sanctified through the offering of the body of Jesus, Heb. 10:10. as the body without the spirit is dead, James 2:26. perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body, James 3:2. bare our sins in his own body on the tree, 1 Pet. 2:24. devil he disputed about the body of Moses, Jude 1:9. dead bodies shall lie in the street, Rev. 11:8.",
